  "basis": "The task requires comparing the 1990 percentage for Urban and Rural and opening the record for the larger category. The chart is a dual-axis plot with 'Urban (%)' on the left and 'Rural (%)' on the right. The O/B checks refuted the visual heuristic that the higher line (Rural) represents a larger value, noting that the Urban axis is scaled much larger (e.g., 0-100%) than the Rural axis. Evidence from the data labels confirms this: the Urban percentage is labeled at 44.20% (1985) and 46.32% (2005), while the Rural percentage is labeled at 12.12% (1985) and 12.57% (2005). The Urban percentage is consistently and significantly larger (approx 3.5x) than the Rural percentage. In 1990, the Urban line is positioned above its 1985 value (44.20%), while the Rural line is positioned above its 1985 value (12.12%). Thus, the Urban percentage is larger.",
  "option_label": "Open 1990 Urban statistics follow-up record"
}
